   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Demon Sweat**: back after 85 archived shows (793 days) [6]\n- **All of My Love**: rare: 9 archived performances [6]\n- **Scary\" Jam**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Fancy Pants**: back after 75 archived shows (617 days); rare: 8 archived performances [6]\n- **Put the Coke on My Dick**: back after 84 archived shows (791 days) [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2003-10-31.aud.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 31 songs; 178 min [1]\n- **ween2003-10-31.mk41.shnf_**: source not stated; 31 songs; 175 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [2]. Said about its sound: The audio recording is described as having very clear sound quality throughout the performance [4]\n- **ween2003-10-31.daud.flac16**: source not stated; 32 songs; 179 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The concert lasted four and a half hours without any set breaks [5]\n- Previous Ween performances were shorter, around three hours, but also lacked set breaks [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2003-10-31.aud.flac16**: taped by Mike Bogigian; transferred by Mike Bogigian; source: Shure SM94's > Balanced Stereo XLR (1/8\" Output) > Sony Minidisc R700 [1]\n- **ween2003-10-31.mk41.shnf_**: taped by PW; transferred by jkeats; source: schoeps mk41>vms>sbm1>dap1 [2]\n- **ween2003-10-31.daud.flac16**: taped by Sean \"Homeslice\" Reardon; transferred by Sean \"Homeslice\" Reardon; source: AT853's(w/hypers)*>Sounpro's Battbox>A/D-20>Hosa Optical>Sony MZ-R700 [3]",
